Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• objects.object_id : join key between `objects` and `vision_api_data`.  
• objects.department : filter to just “The Libraries”.  
• objects.title : check that it includes the word “book”.  
• objects.metadata_date : format as YYYY‑MM‑DD.  
• vision_api_data.object_id : join key.  
• vision_api_data.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints.confidence : filter where confidence > 0.5 (a.k.a. cropConfidence).  

Main conditions you will eventually need  
1. objects.department = 'The Libraries'  
2. LOWER(objects.title) LIKE '%book%'  
3. UNNEST(vision_api_data.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints).confidence > 0.5  

Below are ten exploratory → final BigQuery queries (each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the required answer.

```sql
-- 1) Preview a few rows from the objects table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) See which departments exist
SELECT DISTINCT department
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
ORDER BY department
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Look at objects that belong to “The Libraries”
SELECT object_id, title, metadata_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'The Libraries'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Check titles that already contain the word “book”
SELECT object_id, title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE '%book%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Preview vision_api_data to understand its structure
SELECT object_id, cropHintsAnnotation
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Unnest cropHints to see the confidence values
SELECT
  v.object_id,
  c.confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS c
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Grab object_ids whose crop‑confidence is > 0.5
SELECT DISTINCT v.object_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS c
WHERE c.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Join objects with those high‑confidence images (no title filter yet)
SELECT
  o.object_id,
  o.title,
  o.metadata_date,
  c.confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS c
WHERE c.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same join but add the department requirement
SELECT
  o.object_id,
  o.title,
  o.metadata_date,
  c.confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS c
WHERE o.department = 'The Libraries'
  AND c.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: object_id, title, formatted metadata_date
SELECT DISTINCT
  o.object_id,
  o.title,
  FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%F', o.metadata_date) AS metadata_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS c
WHERE o.department = 'The Libraries'
  AND LOWER(o.title) LIKE '%book%'
  AND c.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```

